# This repository is public. The rule is one line: track only what is certainly
# meant to be public.
#
# So the sections below deny broadly and re-include by name. The other shape — listing
# what to leave out — fails open: a new tool drops a new file and the default is
# "tracked". What lands in history is hard to take back out.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Secrets. A value committed once is a value to treat as burned.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
credentials.json
secrets.json
service-account*.json
*.wallet.json

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. Working notes. Anything meant for readers goes under docs/public/.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/docs/*
!/docs/public/
*.local.md
/scratch/
/sandbox/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. Rust. Narrowed from github/gitignore's template: its bare `debug` and `target`
#    match a directory of that name anywhere, so the day someone adds a `src/debug/`
#    module it disappears without a word. Cargo.lock is tracked on purpose — this
#    workspace produces a binary.
#    `*.crate` is a dependency tarball unpacked for reading; it lands wherever the
#    shell happened to be.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
**/target/
/debug/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
**/mutants.out*/
*.crate
/flamegraph.svg
/perf.data*

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. JavaScript and web, for the day any of it exists.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
/dist/
/build/
.next/
/out/
/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo/
.parcel-cache/
.vite/
.svelte-kit/
.wrangler/
*.wasm
!**/vendor/**/*.wasm

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. Things checking the work leaves behind.
#    Only images dropped at the root. Widening this to `*.png` would swallow the
#    icons the product ships, and a new icon would go missing in silence.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. What machines and editors leave lying around.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
.zed/
.fleet/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Cloudflare
.wrangler/
.dev.vars*
